From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comdlg32: a save dialog is titled "Save As"

Since 0582 GetSaveFileName shows the item dialog, as Windows does since
Vista. That dialog was titled "Save", like its button; Windows titles it
"Save As". Programs and scripts that look for the "Save As" window (UI
automation, a program waiting for its own dialog) found none, and
savedesk-gate's probe waited for it in vain.

The save dialog's title is now "Save As" unless the program sets its own
(SetTitle, or lpstrTitle); the button still says "Save".

Test: test/savedesk-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_SAVE_TITLE in itemdlg.c
fails it).
---
--- a/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
+++ b/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
@@ -4959,8 +4959,15 @@
         fdimpl->options = FOS_OVERWRITEPROMPT | FOS_NOREADONLYRETURN | FOS_PATHMUSTEXIST | FOS_NOCHANGEDIR;
 
         LoadStringW(COMDLG32_hInstance, IDS_SAVE, buf, ARRAY_SIZE(buf));
-        fdimpl->custom_title = StrDupW(buf);
         fdimpl->custom_okbutton = StrDupW(buf);
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_SAVE_TITLE
+        /* Stained Glass OS: a save dialog is titled "Save As", as on Windows
+         * (its button says "Save"). Since 0582 GetSaveFileName shows this
+         * dialog, and scripts and tests that wait for a "Save As" window
+         * (Notepad's, a program's own) found none. */
+        LoadStringW(COMDLG32_hInstance, IDS_SAVE_AS, buf, ARRAY_SIZE(buf));
+#endif
+        fdimpl->custom_title = StrDupW(buf);
     }
 
     list_init(&fdimpl->events_clients);
